sh - the shell

SYNOPSIS
    sh [-c COMMAND] [SCRIPT]

DESCRIPTION
    Reads a line, works out what it says, and runs it.

      quoting        'literal' and "expanded", and \ before one character
      variables      $NAME, ${NAME}, $?, $$, and $1.. inside a script
      assignment     NAME=value, and export to put one in the environment
      patterns       * and ? matched against the filesystem
      lists          ; runs both, && runs the second if the first worked,
                     || runs it if the first did not
      redirection    < > >> 2> 2>>
      pipes          |, any number of stages
      background     a trailing &, with jobs, fg and bg

    Job control is on when there is a terminal. Every job is a process group,
    so Ctrl-C reaches a whole pipeline rather than one stage of it, and Ctrl-Z
    suspends one to be picked up later with fg.

    Builtins: cd exit export unset source : true false jobs fg bg help

SEE ALSO
    kill, ps, env
